---
title: Frijoles Charros
servings: 10
tags:
  - entres
source:
  name: Serious Eats
  url: https://www.seriouseats.com/frijoles-charros-mexican-pinto-beans-bacon-recipe
-- introduction: 
---

= Beans

Rinse and soak @pinto beans{1%lb} with @salt{1%tbsp} and @baking soda{1%tbsp} for ~{12%hours}, thoroughly rinse beans once done soaking.

Bring @pinto beans{} to boil in @stock{6%cups}(optional) with @bay leaves{3}(optional) and @epazote sprigs{3}(optional), then let simmer for ~{45%min}.\
> You can omit the stock and herbs here if you don't have them, still comes out pretty good.

= Gravy

Fry @bacon{0.5%lb}(chopped) in a large skillet or pot.\
> I use scissors to cut them into little pieces.

Add @onion{1}(chopped) and @jalapeno{1}(chopped) and continue frying until they are soft and fragrant.\
> Can substitute serrano or other chili as well, if you want it less spice, be sure to remove all the seeds and pith before chopping.

Add @garlic cloves{3}(minced) and fry for ~{30%sec} (make sure it does not overcook and become bitter).

Add @fire roasted tomatoes{28%oz}(canned) and let simmer until the gravy thickens.
> for a smoother texture, consider running an #?immersion blender{} in the gravy until you get your desired consistency.

= Combine

Add gravy to the cooked beans and let simmer all together for ~{20%min}.

Optionally, use an #immersion blender{} to blender some of the beans so the whole dish is creamier.

= For big batches
Alternatively, you can make a big batch of gravy and freeze it to add to cooked beans later.
If doing so, add the epazote and bay leaves to the gravy.
Fry the bacon, then combine all other ingredients and cook on high for 45 minutes and let it naturally release.
Blend gravy then portion out to freeze.
You can use as little as 1/2 of this gravy recipe for a lb of beans and still have decent results.

